#edb/ref 1074 "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L\\{{e}^{6t}f(t)\\},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $6$ units to the right." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186534962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331796" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a function $z(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L\\{z(t)\\}=Z(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L\\{{e}^{6t}z(t)\\}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{6t}z(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,z(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f860a2b3-6e2b-5a0c-99c8-165c277a9c9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535087 #edb/ref 1074 "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{e}^{6t}z(t)\\} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{6t}\\,z(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-6)t}\\,z(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $Z(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,z(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-6)t}\\,z(t)\\,\\text{d}t=Z(s-6),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-6>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535120 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a11ab2b3-b4ab-5878-9174-f53555687bd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535120 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186535049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535122 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535122 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0e901f2-b8a2-54b2-9949-4ac2f8de516d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535122 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186441316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535123 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535123 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1d2ef25-b3ce-50d5-96e8-d900a85497fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535123 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186304979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535130 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535130 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cece9bbe-7f93-5417-a941-680f66b0cf57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535130 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535136 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186535122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535136 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d715b5d0-cb33-5478-a9fe-0e3da862463c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186535136 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186535087 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
